<title>GREECE: TABLE OF GREEK MUTUAL FUND FLOWS, ASSETS.</title>
<headline>TABLE OF GREEK MUTUAL FUND FLOWS, ASSETS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ionian Bank reported the</p>
<p>following daily and year-to-date changes in the volume of Greek</p>
<p>mutual fund outstanding shares, net assets and net share prices,</p>
<p>as well as total net asset sizes as of July 8.</p>
<p>				  July 08/July 07  July 08/Dec 31, 96</p>
<p>						 (%)		  (%)</p>
<p>NET SHARE PRICES*</p>
<p>  Total market			    0.05		 7.73</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds  0.04		 6.12</p>
<p>  International funds		   0.40		12.10</p>
<p>  Growth Funds			    0.09		52.14</p>
<p>* Prices include distributed dividends</p>
<p>VOLUME OF SHARES</p>
<p>  Total market			   -0.86		37.36</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds -0.90		38.01</p>
<p>  International funds		   0.20		15.13</p>
<p>  Growth funds			    0.07		32.10</p>
<p>NET ASSETS</p>
<p>  Total market			   -0.81		46.20</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds -0.88		44.93</p>
<p>  International funds		   0.66		27.18</p>
<p>  Growth funds			    0.14		95.83</p>
<p>All calculations are based on a performance index of mutual</p>
<p>funds whose base was set to be equal to 100 on December 31,</p>
<p>1991.</p>
<p>NET ASSET SIZES (in drachmas)</p>
<p>  Total market				  5,560,255,136,408</p>
<p>  Fixed income funds			  1,987,902,503,305</p>
<p>  Money market funds			  3,232,135,150,578</p>
<p>  International funds			    99,977,074,475</p>
<p>  Growth funds				    240,240,408,051</p>
<p>--Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
